// Dagolitos, the Aeduan keeper of the depot gate. Sells the way in, and news.
=== start
[flag dago_met] -> again
~ set dago_met
The Aeduan by the fire doesn't get up. He's warming his hands, and his rings, of which there are a great many. "Cadurci," he says pleasantly. "Down from the hills. You're a long way from your mountains, friend, and the wrong side of a war."

"I'm Dagolitos. I keep the gate. The Romans keep what's behind it, and between us we keep the peace."
-> hub

=== again
[flag depot_pass] "Still here? Enjoy the view. Nobody else does."
[!flag depot_pass] "Back again. The gate hasn't moved."
-> hub

